s from the overview are not conflated with internal proof\n26\t  obligations.\n27\t* reject paper-facing blueprint entries that point to declaration names with\n28\t  conditional proof-debt forms such as ``*_of...Obligations``,\n29\t  ``*_of...Residual``, ``*_of...Repair``, ``*_of...Bundle``,\n30\t  ``*_of...Unfaithful``, ``*_assuming...``, ``conditional...``, or\n31\t  ``Conditional...``, even when the declaration header itself has no\n32\t  suspicious public input.\n33\t* classify known faithful boundary-input packages separately, with paper\n34\t  citations, so they do not become indistinguishable from proof debt.\n35\t* optionally, with ``--include-informational-envs``, scan ``definition``,\n36\t  ``remark``, and ``example`` entries as a report-only frontier.  This mode is\n37\t  useful for finding Lean-only construction records advertised near a paper\n38\t  proof without turning those construction records into paper theorem\n39\t  statements.\n40\t\n41\tThe audit is report-only by default.  With ``--ci`` it exits non-zero when a\n42\tfinding is present, unless ``--warn-only`` is also supplied.\n43\t\"\"\"\n44\t\n45\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n46\t\n47\timport argparse\n48\timport json\n49\timport re\n50\timport sys\n51\tfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass\n52\tfrom pathlib import Path\n53\tfrom typing import Sequence\n54\t\n55\tfrom blueprint_lean_sync import (  # noqa: E402\n56\t    BlueprintEntry,\n57\t    LEAN_DECL_RE,\n58\t    LeanDecl,\n59\t    collect_blueprint_entries,\n60\t    collect_lean_decls,\n61\t    strip_lean_comments_preserve_lines,\n62\t)\n63\tfrom lean_header_utils import advance_depth, line_number, starts_keyword\n64\t\n65\t\n66\tTHEOREM_LIKE_ENVS = frozenset({\"theorem\", \"lemma\", \"proposition\", \"corollary\"})\n67\tINFORMATIONAL_ENVS = frozenset({\"definition\", \"remark\", \"example\"})\n68\t\n69\tSTRICT_UPPER_TOKENS = (\n70\t    \"Bridge\",\n71\t    \"Residual\",\n72\t    \"Repair\",\n73\t    \"Package\",\n74\t    \"Pr