/q)$ such that for every\n2095\t\tprojective strategy passing with error $\\eps$ and every joint point family\n2096\t\twith consistency error $\\delta_Q(\\eps)$, the POVM $T^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z}$ of\n2097\t\tDefinition~\\ref{def:concrete-paired-line-measurement} has the two axis-degree\n2098\t\tproperties and consistency defect at most $\\delta_P(\\eps,md/q)$ with that\n2099\t\tpoint family.\n2100\t\\end{lemma}\n2101\t\\begin{proof}\n2102\t\t\\leanok\n2103\t\t\\uses{lem:combined-line-measurement-consistency,\n2104\t\t\tlem:concrete-paired-line-degree-support}\n2105\t\tThe three components are\n2106\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:concrete-paired-line-degree-support} for the two axis-degree\n2107\t\tproperties and Lemma~\\ref{lem:combined-line-measurement-consistency} for the\n2108\t\tconsistency bound, assembled on the explicitly given point family.\n2109\t\\end{proof}\n2110\t\n2111\t\\begin{lemma}[Formalization support: the paired subline overlap]\n2112\t\t\\label{lem:subline-joint-overlap}\n2113\t\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.subline_joint_overlap_near_one_at}\n2114\t\t\\leanok\n2115\t\t\\uses{lem:qld-sublines, lem:claim-17-1, lem:claim-17-2, lem:claim-17-3,\n2116\t\t\tdef:combine-map}\n2117\t\tThere is a constant $c>0$ such that, for every projective strategy with\n2118\t\terror $\\eps$, every joint point family with error $\\delta_Q$, every paired\n2119\t\tline family with error $\\delta_P$, every subline witness, and every directed\n2120\t\topposite placement, the average paired subline overlap differs from $1$ by at\n2121\t\tmost\n2122\t\t\\[\n2123\t\t\tc\\left(\\delta_Q^{1/2}+\\sqrt{m}\\,\n2124\t\t\t\t\\bigl(\\delta_P^{1/4}+\\delta_Q^{1/4}+\\eps^{1/4}\\bigr)\\right).\n2125\t\t\\]\n2126\t\tThis is the first-route estimate of the proof of\n2127\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}, stated for both opposite placements. It compares\n2128\t\treal parts of overlaps; it does not assert the complex modulus comparisons of\n2129\t\tLemmas~\\ref{lem:claim-17-1}--\\ref{lem:claim-17-3} over the source\n2130\t\tdistribution, which remain separate and uncertified. See\n2131\t\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}.\n2132\t\\end{lemma}\n2133\t\\begin{proof}\n2134\t\t\\leanok\n2135\t\t\\uses{lem:qld-sublines, def:combine-map}\n2136\t\tChain the paired-to-ordered overlap gap, the removal of the $X$ factor, and\n2137\t\tthe near-one estimate for the remaining $Z$ term, each taken over the\n2138\t\tdirectly indexed subline law, and collect the resulting quarter powers with\n2139\t\tthe scalar estimate of that chaining."}]},"uuid":"a5610b88-20b8-4bd0-b0e7-65b0c68f126e","timestamp":"2026-09-14T13:25:05.887Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-512-proof-exists-extendedlineswitness-established/blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex","content":"\tneither bound is dominated by a function of $m^2\\eps$ and $md/q$\n\talone that vanishes as its arguments vanish. The proof above\n\ttherefore follows the first route only and establishes the bound\n\t$m \\cdot \\poly(\\eps, md/q)$, which is the form consumed by\n\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-7}, whose error function absorbs the prefactor\n\t$m$ into $(md)^a$. The full analysis --- the two routes, the scalings\n\tshowing that the claimed form follows from neither, the corrected\n\tdeficit assertion in the proof of Lemma~\\ref{lem:claim-17-2}, and the\n\tcandidate repairs with their open obligations --- is given in\n\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}.\n\\end{remark}\n\n\\begin{lemma}[Formalization support: the paired-line construction for a given\n\tpoint family]\n\t\\label{lem:combined-lines-given-points}\n\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_combinedLinesWitness_ofPointsWitness}\n\t\\leanok\n\t\\uses{lem:combined-line-measurement-consistency,\n\t\tdef:concrete-paired-line-measurement,\n\t\tlem:concrete-paired-line-degree-support}\n\tThis formalization-only auxiliary statement displays its point family as an\n\texplicit hypothesis and is therefore not a formalization of\n\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines}, whose statement quantifies the point family\n\texistentially. Fix a polynomially small function $\\delta_Q(\\eps)$. There is\n\ta function $\\delta_P(\\eps,md/q)=\\poly(\\eps,md/q)$ such that for every\n\tprojective strategy passing with error $\\eps$ and every joint point family\n\twith consistency error $\\delta_Q(\\eps)$, the POVM $T^{\\ell_X,\\ell_Z}$ of\n\tDefinition~\\ref{def:concrete-paired-line-measurement} has the two axis-degree\n\tproperties and consistency defect at most $\\delta_P(\\eps,md/q)$ with that\n\tpoint family.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\t\\leanok\n\t\\uses{lem:combined-line-measurement-consistency,\n\t\tlem:concrete-paired-line-degree-support}\n\tThe three components are\n\tLemma~\\ref{lem:concrete-paired-line-degree-support} for the two axis-degree\n\tproperties and Lemma~\\ref{lem:combined-line-measurement-consistency} for the\n\tconsistency bound, assembled on the explicitly given point family.\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\begin{lemma}[Formalization support: the paired subline overlap]\n\t\\label{lem:subline-joint-overlap}\n\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.subline_joint_overlap_near_one_at}\n\t\\leanok\n\t\\uses{lem:qld-sublines, lem:claim-17-1, lem:claim-17-2, lem:claim-17-3,\n\t\tdef:combine-map}\n\tThere is a constant $c>0$ such that, for every projective strategy with\n\terror $\\eps$, every joint point family with error $\\delta_Q$, every paired\n\tline family with error $\\delta_P$, every subline witness, and every directed\n\topposite placement, the average paired subline overlap differs from $1$ by at\n\tmost\n\t\\[\n\t\tc\\left(\\delta_Q^{1/2}+\\sqrt{m}\\,\n\t\t\t\\bigl(\\delta_P^{1/4}+\\delta_Q^{1/4}+\\eps^{1/4}\\bigr)\\right).\n\t\\]\n\tThis is the first-route estimate of the proof of\n\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}, stated for both opposite placements. It compares\n\treal parts of overlaps; it does not assert the complex modulus comparisons of\n\tLemmas~\\ref{lem:claim-17-1}--\\ref{lem:claim-17-3} over the source\n\tdistribution, which remain separate and uncertified. See\n\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\t\\leanok\n\t\\uses{lem:qld-sublines, def:combine-map}\n\tChain the paired-to-ordered overlap gap, the removal of the $X$ factor, and\n\tthe near-one estimate for the remaining $Z$ term, each taken over the\n\tdirectly indexed subline law, and collect the resulting quarter powers with\n\tthe scalar estimate of that chaining.","numLines":70,"startLine":2070,"totalLines":2804}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"19322569-85a0-4c33-aa17-d1133d4674a0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-512-proof-exists-extendedlineswitness-established","sessionId":"4009e4ae-5cba-44c3-9062-7d571f302d36","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"issue-512-proof-exists-extendedlineswitness-established","slug":"unified-doodling-nygaard"}
