 which\n2219\t\tLemma~\\ref{lem:subline-joint-overlap} estimates for both opposite\n2220\t\tplacements; Theorem~\\ref{thm:qld-combining-polynomial-bound} collects the\n2221\t\tresulting quarter powers into the form $m\\cdot\\poly(\\eps,md/q)$, with the\n2222\t\tunit bound on consistency handling large errors. This proves the stated\n2223\t\tdirectly indexed auxiliary.\n2224\t\tApplying it to the source statement remains conditional\n2225\t\ton transporting the question space and distribution and on converting the\n2226\t\tcompleted answer comparison, including zero-direction singleton lines, to\n2227\t\tthe source sum over $a \\in \\F_q$; these obligations are recorded in\n2228\t\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility} and\n2229\t\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}.\n2230\t\\end{proof}\n2231\t\n2232\tThe measurements of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-12} and Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}\n2233\tconstitute a strategy for the classical low individual degree game in $2m+2$\n2234\tvariables. Applying the quantum soundness of that game yields a single\n2235\tprojective measurement whose outcomes are pairs of global polynomials.\n2236\t\n2237\t\\begin{lemma}[The global polynomial-pair measurement]\n2238\t\t\\label{lem:qld-4-7}\n2239\t\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.Poly, MIPStarRE.QPBT.PolyPair, MIPStarRE.QPBT.evalAt}\n2240\t\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.GlobalPairWitness}"}]},"uuid":"a2e447b3-91cd-4eab-93f1-1af86ea2c3ad","timestamp":"2026-09-14T13:27:11.985Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-512-proof-exists-extendedlineswitness-established/blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex","content":"\tpolynomials that admit no evaluation at the sampled point, rather than\n\tunder the answer summation over $a \\in \\F_q$ used above. Thus the auxiliary\n\tconstruction does not establish the source formulation until the question carrier\n\tand law are related by the transport obligation of\n\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility} and the completed answer comparison\n\tis related to the source sum by\n\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\t\\leanok\n\t\\uses{lem:qld-4-10, lem:qld-sublines, lem:combined-lines-given-points,\n\t\tlem:subline-joint-overlap, lem:extended-line-measurement-support,\n\t\tthm:qld-combining-polynomial-bound}\n\tThe formal construction conditions the directly indexed subline law on\n\tthe extended line and averages the combined polynomial outcomes of the\n\tconstructed $X$-$Z$-$X$ line measurement. The point family is the one\n\tsupplied by Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-10}; applied to it, the conditional\n\tconstruction of Lemma~\\ref{lem:combined-lines-given-points} produces the\n\tpaired line family, so that construction enters here as a formalization\n\tauxiliary with its point family already fixed, not as a certification of\n\tLemma~\\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines}. The two properties of\n\tLemma~\\ref{lem:extended-line-measurement-support} give the degree support\n\tand reduce both consistency displays to the paired subline overlap, which\n\tLemma~\\ref{lem:subline-joint-overlap} estimates for both opposite\n\tplacements; Theorem~\\ref{thm:qld-combining-polynomial-bound} collects the\n\tresulting quarter powers into the form $m\\cdot\\poly(\\eps,md/q)$, with the\n\tunit bound on consistency handling large errors. This proves the stated\n\tdirectly indexed auxiliary.\n\tApplying it to the source statement remains conditional\n\ton transporting the question space and distribution and on converting the\n\tcompleted answer comparison, including zero-direction singleton lines, to\n\tthe source sum over $a \\in \\F_q$; these obligations are recorded in\n\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility} and\n\t\\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}.\n\\end{proof}\n\nThe measurements of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-12} and Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}\nconstitute a strategy for the classical low individual degree game in $2m+2$\nvariables. Applying the quantum soundness of that game yields a single\nprojective measurement whose outcomes are pairs of global polynomials.\n\n\\begin{lemma}[The global polynomial-pair measurement]\n\t\\label{lem:qld-4-7}\n\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.Poly, MIPStarRE.QPBT.PolyPair, MIPStarRE.QPBT.evalAt}\n\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.GlobalPairWitness}","numLines":45,"startLine":2196,"totalLines":2804}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a2bded26-975b-42ff-8ee1-98fec1eaac03","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-512-proof-exists-extendedlineswitness-established","sessionId":"4009e4ae-5cba-44c3-9062-7d571f302d36","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"issue-512-proof-exists-extendedlineswitness-established","slug":"unified-doodling-nygaard"}
