/home/drx/.cache/mipstarre-dev/reviews/pr549/reviews.json:26:  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=549 head=aeaca3aee589ff666c5ab6feb2681e2cb06e8b1d -->\n# Review \u2014 PR 549 @ aeaca3aee589\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=CHANGES_REQUESTED, prose=CHANGES_REQUESTED)\n\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-14T12:58:59Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\n\nBranch `issue-512-proof-exists-extendedlineswitness-established` onto `main`; merge base `ae124f8f09ee002444ac5b9711822c0f1daae142`; head `aeaca3aee589ff666c5ab6feb2681e2cb06e8b1d`.\n\n## Findings\n\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 (changes) `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex:398` \u2014 The note still says both proofs are open and neither node is formalized, although this PR proves and marks the established auxiliary `\\leanok`.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `audits/2026-09-12-issue512-saved-proof-recovery.md:1` \u2014 The new audit omits the mandatory YAML metadata and required audit structure, and its filename violates the `YYYY-MM-DD_` convention.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F3 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Claims.lean:40` \u2014 Two generic scalar helpers are promoted into the public API without docstrings or an appropriate scalar-utility module boundary.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F4 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/Conditioning.lean:325` \u2014 The module ends with an empty section and a scoped `open DistanceCalculus in` that applies only to `end`.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F5 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1053` \u2014 The new statement-level `\\leanok` omits the Lean theorem\u2019s completed optional answer alphabet, making the blueprint statement weaker.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F6 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1038` \u2014 The completed `combined_line_measurement_consistency` proof lacks a proof-level `\\leanok` block.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F7 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1039` \u2014 The consistency theorem\u2019s `\\uses` are attached to its statement and omit the Lean proof\u2019s direct restored-defect and error-bound dependencies.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F8 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:2051` \u2014 The extended-line proof\u2019s `\\uses` names source results instead of its actual conditional and auxiliary dependencies.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F9 (changes) `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex:398` \u2014 Status prose still says both extended-line proofs are open and neither node is marked formalized.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F10 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/ExtendedLines/Estimates.lean:15` \u2014 Repeated \u201cRecovered from commit \u2026 for issue #512\u201d text records implementation history in reader-facing docstrings.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F11 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1041` \u2014 \u201cLean-only construction theorem\u201d is Lean jargon in the blueprint and corresponding Lean docstring.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F12 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/Conditioning.lean:31` \u2014 \u201cformalization-only adapter\u201d is software terminology; use \u201cformalization-only auxiliary lemma.\u201d  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F13 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/Sampling.lean:106` \u2014 \u201craw direction coordinate\u201d uses process-shaped terminology; use \u201csampled direction coordinate.\u201d  <!-- lane=prose -->\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Code review\n\nF1 must be corrected to reflect the present state. `exists_extendedLinesWitness_established` is now proved at `Apply.lean:147`, and blueprint `lem:qld-4-13-established` carries statement and proof `\\leanok` at `ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:2019,2050`. Thus \u201cBoth proofs are open\u201d is false, as is the later assertion that neither blueprint node carries a formalization mark. The note should distinguish the still-open source-shaped `exists_extendedLinesWitness` from the completed directly indexed auxiliary. Paper-gap policy requires revisions to remain a coherent account of the current mathematical status.\n\nF2 violates the active format in `audits/2026-04-29_audit-document-format.md`: new audits require YAML front matter, `YYYY-MM-DD_` filenames, and an explicit review-oriented structure. Add at least `title`, `date`, `purpose`, `issue`, and `pr`, reorganize or justify the narrower section structure, and update the paper-gap reference if the file is renamed.\n\nF3 broadens `rpow_quarter_nonneg` and `sqrt_deficit_bound_le` from private implementation details into reusable declarations solely so `ExtendedLines/Estimates.lean` can import them. They now need mathematical docstrings. Since neither is specific to Claims 17-1 through 17-3, the cleaner boundary is `ErrorBounds.lean` or a focused scalar-estimates module, avoiding an unnecessary dependency on the claims module and its retained proof obligation.\n\nF4 is extraction residue. The \u201cUnequal-dimensional bipartite transport\u201d section contains no declarations, while `open DistanceCalculus in` scopes only the closing `end`. Remove it or move the heading to `Lines/Construction.lean`, where the bipartition transport declarations actually live.\n\nMathematically, I found no source-statement blocker. Paper `lem:qld-xz-lines` at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:882-894,942-961` constructs the same X-Z-X measurement, and the proof-only conditioning is explicitly restored to the original product law. Paper `lem:qld-4-13` at lines 1020-1034 remains separate and unproved. Blueprint `lem:qld-4-13-established` explicitly records the direct carrier/law, completed answers, and weaker \\(C m\\,\\mathrm{poly}(\\epsilon,md/q)\\) error, so it does not misrepresent the source theorem.\n\n`lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Apply.lean` passed. Its four `sorry` warnings and the retained `subline_remove_X_factor_direct` hole are all clearly documented as known obligations; no unmarked proof hole or unsafe proof mechanism was found.\n\n## Prose review\n\nF1: The Lean conclusion at `Lines/Construction.lean:435-445` postprocesses line answers using `evalOpt` into `Option \u00d7 Option` and embeds point answers with `some`. Undefined line evaluations therefore contribute to the off-diagonal defect. The blueprint must explicitly state the completed alphabet \\((\\F_q\\cup\\{\\bot\\})^2\\) and the zero extension of the point measurement before its statement-level `\\leanok` is valid.\n\nF2: The marker at line 1038 is inside the lemma environment, so it certifies only the statement. Add a separate proof environment with `\\leanok`; the Lean proof at `Lines/Construction.lean:429-492` has no `sorryAx`.\n\nF3: The Lean proof directly invokes `exists_combinedLine_restored_defect_le` and `exists_conditioned_polynomial_bound`. The current statement-level dependencies instead list `lem:qld-comm-line-cons` and `lem:pasting`, which are transitive proof inputs. Add a subordinate support node for the restored-defect theorem, use `thm:qld-conditioned-polynomial-bound` in the proof dependencies, and keep statement dependencies minimal.\n\nF4: `Apply.lean:157-196` directly uses `exists_combinedPointsWitness`, the existing conditional `_ofPointsWitness` construction, `subline_joint_overlap_near_one_at`, `exists_combining_polynomial_bound`, and the extended-line consistency and degree results. It does not call `lem:qld-4-12`. Record the conditional helper and new public auxiliaries in separate formalization-support nodes, without placing them on a source-labelled `\\leanok` path, and include `lem:qld-4-10` plus `thm:qld-combining-polynomial-bound`.\n\nF5: Lines 398 and 410 contradict the new statement/proof markers at blueprint lines 2019 and 2050. State that only the printed-error declaration remains open; the established auxiliary is proved and marked. The same stale claim also remains in `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt-gap-register.md:17`.\n\nF6: Remove the recovery provenance from the module and theorem docstrings, retaining only mathematical source and gap references. The pattern recurs across `ExtendedLines/{Estimates,Measurement,Overlap}`, `Lines/{Conditioning,Construction,PointComparison,Sampling}`, `SubLineXDeficit`, `XEvalDeficit`, and at `Lines.lean:61,102` and `Lines/Construction.lean:426`.\n\nF7: Replace \u201cLean-only construction theorem\u201d with \u201cformalization-only auxiliary theorem.\u201d Apply the same correction to `Lines/Construction.lean:414`.\n\nF8: Replace the sentence with \u201cThis formalization-only auxiliary lemma is applied below with the proved fiber estimate.\u201d\n\nF9: Replace \u201cthe last raw direction coordinate\u201d with \u201cthe last sampled direction coordinate.\u201d\n\nThe ordered \\(X\\)-then-\\(Z\\) addition matches its Lean signature. The separate established extended-line statement also accurately records its directly indexed carrier, completed answers, and corrected error. The source-labelled `lem:qld-xz-lines` and `lem:qld-4-13` entries should remain `\\notready`.\n\nCounts: 1 equivalence mismatch, 3 blueprint status/dependency issues, 1 stale status record, and 4 prose issues.\n",
/home/drx/.cache/mipstarre-dev/reviews/pr549/reviews.json:66:  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=549 head=aef4744203e113d96d002171ead423d135afada8 -->\n# Review \u2014 PR 549 @ aef4744203e1\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=CHANGES_REQUESTED, prose=CHANGES_REQUESTED)\n\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-15T02:55:55Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\n\nBranch `issue-512-proof-exists-extendedlineswitness-established` onto `main`; merge base `36cf9d5db7c47132f0be1fbab68d9dbef2c5776f`; head `aef4744203e113d96d002171ead423d135afada8`.\n\n## Findings\n\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 (blocker) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Apply.lean:136` \u2014 `exists_extendedLinesWitness_established_ofPointsWitness` retains an unmarked `sorry` for a known-false arbitrary-`\u03b4Q` statement.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1070` \u2014 The restored-defect proof derives a `1/(2q)` cost from only a stated `1/q` discarded probability.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F3 (changes) `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_subline-claims-line-marginal.tex:173` \u2014 The note incorrectly calls `CombinedLinesWitness` source-faithful despite its unresolved completed-`Option` answer comparison.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F4 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:2093` \u2014 The certified conditional node is not signature-equivalent to `exists_combinedLinesWitness_ofPointsWitness`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F5 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1070` \u2014 The proof derives a `1/(2q)` restoration cost from only a stated `1/q` event bound.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F6 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:2118` \u2014 The new `\\uses` edges cite `\\notready` source nodes and omit the directly indexed declarations actually invoked.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F7 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:2116` \u2014 The certified support blocks lack blueprint entries for the new overlap and extended-measurement definitions they state.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F8 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:2099` \u2014 Status prose uses private workflow language such as \u201cquarantined,\u201d \u201cformalization-support node,\u201d and \u201cformalization mark.\u201d  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F9 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/Conditioning.lean:119` \u2014 The comment describes a Lean \u201cnormalization goal\u201d rather than the mathematical normalization.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F10 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/ExtendedLines/Measurement.lean:108` \u2014 The docstrings use control-flow language including \u201czero-mass branch\u201d and \u201cfield-valued fallback.\u201d  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F11 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/ExtendedLines/Estimates.lean:30` \u2014 `BBprime` and `ABdoubleprime` expose private identifier spellings instead of the paper\u2019s register notation.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F12 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/ExtendedLines/Estimates.lean:8` \u2014 Repeated module prose says conventions \u201cretain their existing meanings\u201d instead of stating those conventions mathematically.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F13 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/Sampling.lean:33` \u2014 Several new docstrings use process-shaped \u201cproof-only\u201d terminology instead of \u201cformalization-only auxiliary.\u201d  <!-- lane=prose -->\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Code review\n\nF1 must be fixed before merge. The statement of `exists_extendedLinesWitness_established_ofPointsWitness` accepts an arbitrary scalar `\u03b4Q`, while its output error does not depend on that scalar. `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex:217-289` documents this obstruction, including issue #511 and the failure of the unrestricted supplied-point auxiliary. Nevertheless, the theorem\u2019s docstring presents it as a construction obligation and gives neither the required `**Unfaithful:**` marker nor a discharge or deletion plan. The module summary also says only the printed-error and global-pair assertions remain open. Add the prescribed marker, cite the gap and issue, and state that the helper must be restricted to polynomially controlled point errors or removed.\n\nF2 requires a mathematical correction. The blueprint says the discarded event has probability at most `1/q`, then concludes that restoring it costs at most `1/(2q)`. That conclusion does not follow from the stated premise. The Lean proof in `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/Sampling.lean:79-90` obtains the sharper factor from the equal axis/diagonal mixture: the axis component contributes zero and only half of the diagonal zero-direction mass remains. The blueprint proof should state that argument or directly state the `1/(2q)` bound.\n\nF3 requires a more precise verdict in the changed paper-gap note. Paper `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:882-893` formulates `lem:qld-xz-lines` with field-valued evaluations, whereas `CombinedLinesWitness.consistent` in `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Witnesses.lean:118-131` compares completed `Option` answers. The corresponding blueprint node `lem:qld-xz-lines` remains not ready because this transport is unresolved. The note should describe the record as capturing the concrete measurement and degree data while retaining a completed-answer deviation, not as faithfully expressing the source conclusion.\n\nThe new proof of `exists_extendedLinesWitness_established` otherwise has a coherent dependency chain: it constructs the point and line witnesses, uses the genuine conditional extended-line measurement, proves both placement estimates, and applies the scalar absorption lemma. Its direct carrier, completed answer alphabet, and weaker established error are all displayed explicitly by blueprint support node `lem:qld-4-13-established`; it is not being advertised as the printed source theorem.\n\nTargeted Lean checks of `Apply.lean`, `Lines/Construction.lean`, and `ExtendedLines/Estimates.lean` passed. The target theorem and its new dependencies report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound` under `#print axioms`. Prior-round findings F1-F13 were addressed; the remaining findings above concern the current documentation and proof-status contracts.\n\n## Prose review\n\n**F1:** The blueprint assumes only \u201ca joint point family with consistency error,\u201d while the Lean theorem requires the complete `CombinedPointsWitness` contract from `Witnesses.lean:59`, including projectivity and all three consistency estimates. More importantly, the blueprint asserts that the concrete POVM has the properties, whereas `Lines.lean:85` returns only `Nonempty (CombinedLinesWitness ...)`; its public signature does not constrain the witness field `T` to equal `combinedLineMeasurement`. Restate the block existentially, display the full completed-answer and opposite-placement contract, and reserve identification with the concrete POVM for the proof.\n\n**F2:** `Lines/Sampling.lean:132` proves the discarded event itself has mass at most `1/(2q)`. The blueprint\u2019s weaker `1/q` statement does not imply the claimed `1/(2q)` cost. Change the probability bound to `1/(2q)` and mention the equal axis/diagonal mixture.\n\n**F3:** Lines 2118, 2138, 2151, 2165, and 2235 point certified proofs through `lem:qld-sublines` and Claims 17-1 through 17-3, although those source nodes remain `\\notready`. The Lean proofs instead use the directly indexed law and helpers such as `subline_remove_X_factor_at`, `subline_Z_term_near_one_at`, `paired_ordered_overlap_gap_le`, and `exists_subLineWitness`. Add certified support entries for the direct declarations and make the `\\uses` graph reflect those dependencies.\n\n**F4:** `pairedSublineOverlap` at `ExtendedLines/Overlap.lean:252` and `SubLineWitness.extendedMeasurement` at `ExtendedLines/Measurement.lean:173` are new public mathematical definitions explicitly described by the support blocks, but neither has a blueprint `\\lean{...}` entry. State and link these definitions before certifying the dependent results.\n\n**F5:** Replace the process paragraph with direct status prose, for example: \u201cBecause the joint point family is an explicit hypothesis, this auxiliary is separate from Lemma qld-xz-lines and does not prove that source lemma.\u201d Likewise replace \u201cuncertified,\u201d \u201csource-shaped replacement,\u201d and \u201ccertification\u201d at lines 2133, 2210, and 2244 with direct mathematical assertions.\n\n**F6:** Drop the comment or say, \u201cExpanding the conditioned product law gives the corresponding finite normalization identity.\u201d\n\n**F7:** Replace \u201cThere is no zero-mass branch\u201d with \u201cEvery extended line has positive marginal mass.\u201d At line 254, replace \u201cassigning a field-valued fallback\u201d with \u201cassigning an arbitrary field value.\u201d\n\n**F8:** Use the paper notation, such as \u201cBob\u2019s \\(BB'\\) registers and Alice\u2019s \\(AB''\\) registers.\u201d\n\n**F9:** The same vague historical sentence occurs in five new modules. State concretely that the construction uses the directly indexed line space, the completed answer alphabet, and the corrected sum-form polynomial error convention.\n\n**F10:** Replace the new \u201cproof-only\u201d occurrences in `Sampling.lean`, `Conditioning.lean`, and `Construction.lean` with \u201cformalization-only auxiliary,\u201d followed by the paper equation or construction each result supports.\n\nThe prior completed-answer and newly closed-proof status issues are otherwise resolved. The source `\\notready` tags for `lem:qld-xz-lines`, `lem:qld-sublines`, and `lem:qld-4-13` remain appropriate. Counts: 1 signature-equivalence blocker, 3 additional synchronization/status findings, and 6 prose findings.\n",
/home/drx/.cache/mipstarre-dev/reviews/pr549/reviews.json:106:  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=549 head=20149b2510f74581fc5e48efbb93f18ab4441676 -->\n# Review \u2014 PR 549 @ 20149b2510f7\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=APPROVED, prose=CHANGES_REQUESTED)\n\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-15T04:16:12Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\n\nBranch `issue-512-proof-exists-extendedlineswitness-established` onto `main`; merge base `36cf9d5db7c47132f0be1fbab68d9dbef2c5776f`; head `20149b2510f74581fc5e48efbb93f18ab4441676`.\n\n## Findings\n\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1380` \u2014 `lem:qld-sublines` links a directly indexed replacement that is not mathematically equivalent to the source lemma.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F2 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1046` \u2014 The restored-defect blueprint statement omits the full point-family hypotheses required by the Lean signature.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Code review\n\nNo blocker or requires-changes issue remains.\n\nThe new `exists_extendedLinesWitness_established` proof is grounded in the concrete point, line, subline, overlap, and scalar-bound constructions. Its axiom closure contains only standard axioms and no `sorryAx`.\n\nSource fidelity is preserved. The printed theorem `lem:qld-4-13` from `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1020-1034` remains explicitly unfinished. The separate blueprint node `lem:qld-4-13-established` accurately states the directly indexed carrier, completed answer alphabet, and established error bound.\n\nThe unrestricted supplied-point helper is now clearly marked `**Unfaithful:**`, documents why it is false, cites issue #511, and is not used by the completed proof. All remaining `sorry` occurrences in the touched modules are similarly documented known obligations; this PR introduces none.\n\nValidation completed successfully for the principal changed Lean modules, including `Apply.lean`, `Claims.lean`, line construction, conditioning, point comparison, extended measurement, and estimates. `lake exe checkdecls blueprint/lean_decls` resolved all 1456 declarations, `git diff --check` passed, and the added-line proof-integrity scan found no forbidden constructs.\n\n## Prose review\n\n**F1.** The source-labelled `lem:qld-sublines` links `MIPStarRE.QPBT.SubLineWitness`. However, that structure at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Witnesses.lean:201` uses `DirectLineDesc`, `directLinePointDist`, and separate projected marginals. The source lemma instead concerns the seed-indexed line law on the original extended space. The directly indexed structure is already represented accurately by `def:direct-subline-law` at line 1633 and its existence theorem at line 1676. Remove this `\\lean{...}` from `lem:qld-sublines` and retain `\\notready`.\n\n**F2.** The blueprint assumes only that \u201ca joint point family have consistency error \\(\\delta_Q\\).\u201d The Lean theorem `exists_combinedLine_restored_defect_le` at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/Construction.lean:294` requires a `CombinedPointsWitness`. Its definition at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Witnesses.lean:59` additionally includes complete projective measurements, self-consistency, and both ordered \\(XZ\\) and \\(ZX\\) comparison bounds. State that the family satisfies all conclusions of `lem:qld-4-10`, and record that dependency in `\\uses`; until then, the statement-level `\\leanok` is inaccurate.\n\nThe remaining new proof-status tags correspond to closed declarations. I found no category-B prose issues. Totals: **2 equivalence/status issues, 0 prose issues**. The attached prior ledger had no visible entries because of truncation, so earlier findings could not be deduplicated from it.\n",
