 why it is false, cites issue #511, and is not used by the completed proof. All remaining `sorry` occurrences in the touched modules are similarly documented known obligations; this PR introduces none.\n\nValidation completed successfully for the principal changed Lean modules, including `Apply.lean`, `Claims.lean`, line construction, conditioning, point comparison, extended measurement, and estimates. `lake exe checkdecls blueprint/lean_decls` resolved all 1456 declarations, `git diff --check` passed, and the added-line proof-integrity scan found no forbidden constructs.\n\n## Prose review\n\n**F1.** The source-labelled `lem:qld-sublines` links `MIPStarRE.QPBT.SubLineWitness`. However, that structure at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Witnesses.lean:201` uses `DirectLineDesc`, `directLinePointDist`, and separate projected marginals. The source lemma instead concerns the seed-indexed line law on the original extended space. The directly indexed structure is already represented accurately by `def:direct-subline-law` at line 1633 and its existence theorem at line 1676. Remove this `\\lean{...}` from `lem:qld-sublines` and retain `\\notready`.\n\n**F2.** The blueprint assumes only that \u201ca joint point family have consistency error \\(\\delta_Q\\).\u201d The Lean theorem `exists_combinedLine_restored_defect_le` at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/Construction.lean:294` requires a `CombinedPointsWitness`. Its definition at `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Witnesses.lean:59` additionally includes complete projective measurements, self-consistency, and both ordered \\(XZ\\) and \\(ZX\\) comparison bounds. State that the family satisfies all conclusions of `lem:qld-4-10`, and record that dependency in `\\uses`; until then, the statement-level `\\leanok` is inaccurate.\n\nThe remaining new proof-status tags correspond to closed declarations. I found no category-B prose issues. Totals: **2 equivalence/status issues, 0 prose issues**. The attached prior ledger had no visible entries because of truncation, so earlier findings could not be deduplicated from it.\n",
